KigaliFleet — Public Storefront Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Version 1.0 · 9 November 2026 · Product specification for implementation

This document defines how the public storefront should work when a vehicle rental or transport company shares its KigaliFleet link with customers.

Important distinction: This is the target product specification, not a claim that these features already exist in the current MVP. Existing functionality must be inspected before implementation. Do not delete or replace working features simply to match this document.
Implementation specification
1. Product definition
KigaliFleet's storefront is a public-facing booking website for each transport or vehicle-rental business using the platform.

Each business gets its own branded page and booking experience.

Example:

kigalifleet.vercel.app/booking/green-rides

A customer opens the link, explores the business, checks available vehicles or services, submits a booking, receives confirmation, and can track or manage their booking.

The storefront has three connected parts:
1. Business website: Shows the company, vehicles, services, policies and contact information.
2. Booking engine: Handles availability, pricing, booking requests and payment.
3. Customer service system: Handles confirmations, vouchers, support and booking updates.
All three must connect to the company's KigaliFleet dashboard.
2. Product objectives
Objective	Expected result
Build trust	Customers understand who they are booking with
Discover services	Customers can find the right vehicle or transport service
Book easily	Customers can submit a booking without unnecessary steps
Show accurate prices	Customers understand what they will pay
Confirm bookings	Customers know whether a booking is requested or confirmed
Support customers	Customers can contact the company and resolve problems
