6. Special booking workflows
These workflows should not be treated as identical.
A. Self-drive rental
1. Customer selects a vehicle.
2. Customer chooses pickup and return dates.
3. System checks vehicle availability.
4. System calculates the rental price and deposit.
5. Customer provides required details.
6. Customer submits the booking or completes instant booking.
7. Company receives the booking in its dashboard.
8. Customer receives the appropriate confirmation.
B. Airport transfer








skybridgecars.com


Additional information:
- Airport
- Flight number
- Airline
- Arrival date and time
- Passenger count
- Luggage count
- Destination
- Contact phone
- Special requirements
The company should be able to see this information before assigning a driver.

Flight tracking can be added later. Do not make an external flight API a launch dependency.
C. Chauffeur-driven transport
Additional information:
- Pickup location
- Destination
- Journey date
- Start time
- Expected duration
- Passenger count
- Itinerary
- Special instructions
Pricing may depend on time, distance, route or a company quotation.
D. Corporate booking
A corporate customer may need:
- Company name
- Organization contact
- Multiple vehicles
- Multiple passengers
- Quote request
- Purchase order reference
- Invoice
- Approval process
Start with a request-and-quotation workflow. A full corporate account system can come later.
E. Group and tour booking
For multi-day trips, multiple vehicles or custom itineraries, allow a quote request rather than pretending a simple vehicle booking can calculate every cost.

7. Pricing and availability engine
This is a critical backend requirement.
Pricing inputs
The pricing engine should support configurable rules such as:
- Daily rental rate
- Hourly rate
- Rental duration
- Weekend pricing
- Seasonal pricing
- Chauffeur fee
- Distance fee
- Pickup or drop-off fee
- Additional services
- Discounts
- Taxes
- Deposit
- Late return fee
Not every business needs every rule.
Availability rules
The system must consider:
- Vehicle bookings
- Temporary booking holds
- Maintenance schedules
- Vehicle operational status
- Pickup and return buffers
- Driver availability for chauffeur services
Technical rule: availability must be checked again on the server when the customer submits the booking. Two customers must not be able to confirm the same vehicle for overlapping dates.

Temporary holds must expire and release the vehicle when the customer abandons checkout.

8. Payments and financial confirmation
Payment integration should be configurable by business.

Potential methods:
- MTN Mobile Money
- Airtel Money
- Bank transfer
- Card payment
- Manual payment confirmation
Do not show a payment method as available until the company has configured and tested it.
Payment lifecycle
Stage	Expected system behavior
Payment initiated	Record payment attempt
Awaiting response	Show pending
Successful	Verify through trusted server-side provider response
Failed	Show failure and retry option
Cancelled	Record cancellation
Refund requested	Record refund request
Refunded	Update refund status after verification

Never trust a browser redirect as proof of payment.

A booking and a payment are separate records. One booking may have multiple payment attempts or partial payments.

